                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "g5SeO",
                  "name": "Desc",
                  "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1200,
                  "content": "IncomeLine is “free-typed” (§10.6) and TransferLine carries “a manual adjustment” (§7.5), but neither input was specified. The review notice is the only defence ADR-0007 has against a wrong Auto amount, so it becomes tappable rather than merely dismissible. Un-ticking Done deletes the Expense it created, behind a confirmation. Plus the two states named but never drawn: the very first plan, and a negative Sisa.",
